SUMMARY:(390) Alma hides a mag 11.4 star (just outside the path)
DESCRIPTION:(390) Alma hides a magnitude 11.4 star\, seen from Vellore.\nTh
 e predicted edge passes 7 km to the S\, so a miss is likely — but a chor
 d from near the edge is the most valuable observation of all.\nClosest app
 roach 22:34:42 IST\, give or take 2 s. The star is 29° up in the ENE · d
 ark sky.\nIt fades 3.4 magnitudes for up to 4.1 s on the centre line\, and
  the path is 26 km wide\, give or take 15 km.\nFinder chart\, the map and 
 the path as KML: https://occult.alokm.com/asteroids-2026-09#2026-09-10-390
 -alma-580096
